 "method": {
  "timing": "Three repetitions per case, each a fresh process, cases interleaved with the order reversed on the middle repetition; all seven thread pools pinned to 1; the one-minute load average before each run is recorded. wall_s/cpu_s time the operation only (warmup and data build excluded); peak_rss_mb is the process high-water mark (ru_maxrss), peak_rss_before_operation_mb the same mark just before the operation. reml_search_cost reports its own per-leg wall and sampled peak RSS, and no CPU time.",
  "profiling": "A separate run: benchmarks/tweedie_estimate_p_timing.py --buckets wraps the functions in BUCKET_TARGETS and charges wall time to the outermost bucket entered (candidate fits: fit_irls_direct, fit_pirls, SuperGLM.fit_reml, the fit_ops publication refits; phi/density: _profile_phi_detailed, _evaluate_tweedie_density, the joint kernel). reml_scale_inside_fits_s is profile_tweedie_reml_scale, timed on its own clock inside candidate fits.",
  "commands": {
   "zeros90_fit": "uv run python benchmarks/tweedie_estimate_p_timing.py --case zeros90 --fit-mode fit",
   "zeros90_reml": "uv run python benchmarks/tweedie_estimate_p_timing.py --case zeros90 --fit-mode reml",
   "positive96_fit": "uv run python benchmarks/tweedie_estimate_p_timing.py --case positive96 --fit-mode fit",
   "positive96_reml": "uv run python benchmarks/tweedie_estimate_p_timing.py --case positive96 --fit-mode reml",
